[TEXT] Clear evidence found. Root cause identified on router6:

- pc15 → 172.18.51.254 (gateway): **works** — local link fine, gateway reachable
- iptables FORWARD chain on router6: **DROP rules on eth2 (WAN interface)** blocking all inbound TCP, UDP, ICMP (24 ICMP pkts already dropped)
- Only exception: ACCEPT tcp in=eth2 src=172.16.10.0/24 dst=172.18.51.1 dport=80

The ACL drops all forwarded traffic arriving on eth2. Outbound packets (from 172.18.51.x leaving via eth2) pass unhindered but return/inbound traffic is blocked. Same mechanism blocks external hosts trying to reach 172.18.51.x via eth2.

No routing fault — router6 has a valid default route via 10.50.1.1 (router3).

